              },
              "question": "<p>Choose the statement(s) about bisphosphonates that is/are correct.</p>\n"
            },
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "metadata": {
              "contentType": "Multiple Choice",
              "license": "U",
              "title": "Untitled Multiple Choice"
            },
            "subContentId": "69c7f9fd-b173-48dd-9b59-55f5f713eec3"
          },
          {
            "params": {
              "media": {
                "disableImageZooming": false
              },
              "answers": [
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Teriparatide is an anabolic drug, meaning that it “builds up” and in this case, it builds bone. \n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Teriparatide is a recumbent form of parathyroid hormone (PTH), so it acts like PTH, activating osteoblasts more than osteoclasts.\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Because teriparatide acts like PTH, it decreases renal excretion of calcium by the kidneys, and increases absorption of calcium in the gut, potentially leading to hypercalcaemia, so calcium levels should be monitored.&nbsp;\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "chosenFeedback": "This statement is incorrect, as daily subcutaneous (SC) injections are needed\n",
                    "notChosenFeedback": "This statement is incorrect, as daily subcutaneous (SC) injections are needed\n",
                    "tip": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Teriparatide is an oral medication\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Teriparatide is used off label for speeding up bone fractures, especially in athletes. \n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "There is a slight increased risk of developing bone cancer (osteosarcoma) with use of teriparatide. \n"
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 100
                }
              ],
